  "main_result": "Native cyclic two-run source detection, nonzero-minor annihilation under the already verified knot-group torsion-free premise, independent v9 source replay, and polynomial raw deletion epochs.",
  "performance": "Initial discovery introduced 3-7 percent survivor overhead. Exact coherent-candidate eligibility guard removes all detector work in the source audit. Guarded full-call paired ratios 0.976 to 1.021; Gordian work exactly 842290 in both engines. No broad speedup or automatic corpus coverage gain.",
  "scope": "Binary capacity fixtures are supplied presentations with power parameter b through 4096 (4097-bit exponents), not hard PDs. The complete PD proof uses a deliberately supplied two-Whitehead prefix. Broader conjugacy graphs and global quasi-polynomial recognition remain unimplemented.",
  "primary_reference": {
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.00621",
    "verified_statement": "Lemma 2.3, arXiv v1: nontrivial knot-group elements conjugate between powers have equal absolute exponents. This stronger balancedness fact is not needed by the native plain-power rule."
